KG42.register("source_edge_archive-748b266b159207cbad64671e",{"id":"13-consensus_product_differentiation::v141-c-R001::E::v141-c-R001-E002","paper":"13-consensus_product_differentiation","rule_id":"v141-c-R001","rule_ref":"13-consensus_product_differentiation::v141-c-R001","record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R001-E002","source":"coordination.price_signal","target":"bidding.demand","type":"precedes","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R001-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g01-e18","v141-b-g01-e33"]},"evidence_class":"S","provenance_gate":"direct_C_edge_with_constraint_and_source_excerpt","scientific_acceptance":false,"accepted_constraint_ids":["v141-c-R001-C002"],"held_constraint_ids":[],"semantic_review_status":"supported","source":"COMP-fe1c33d7a61b4b97","target":"COMP-b9841ac99d9d29b8","source_occurrence_id":"13-consensus_product_differentiation::v141-c-R001::V::coordination.price_signal","target_occurrence_id":"13-consensus_product_differentiation::v141-c-R001::V::bidding.demand","source_unit_id":"13-consensus_product_differentiation::M01::coordination.price_signal","target_unit_id":"13-consensus_product_differentiation::M01::bidding.demand","omega":{"market_type":"DEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"bidding","context_text":"Communication of consumer quantity estimates during decentralized RCI negotiation. | Consumer requested-energy quantities in MBED and their iterative RCI updates. | Feasibility of consumer requested quantities in MBED. | Sequence of updates within an RCI iteration, restricted to the requested-energy decision variables of consumers. | Target-setpoint calculation for the consumer branch of decentralized RCI negotiation. | The discussed direct-solution alternative for consumer local MBED subproblems, rather than the implemented RCI gradient update.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g01-e06","v141-b-g01-e07","v141-b-g01-e18","v141-b-g01-e23","v141-b-g01-e28","v141-b-g01-e32","v141-b-g01-e33","v141-b-g02-e14","v141-b-g02-e15","v141-b-g02-e19"]},"active":true,"source_signature":"8f48a498c463036dd678d70d7fb898d6fdc18d412599eeb60e310092a7e2327e","relation_scope":"original_occurrence_pair_only","internal_to_parent":false,"source_science":{"mechanism_id":"M01","source_definition":"The producer's current offered bilateral quantity enters the price-estimate update through the trading-reciprocity imbalance term. Scope: Producer-side quantity feedback in decentralized MBED forward-market negotiation. Condition: During an RCI price update involving a producer's bilateral quantity. The consumer's current requested bilateral quantity enters the price-estimate update through the trading-reciprocity imbalance term. Scope: Consumer-side quantity feedback in decentralized MBED forward-market negotiation. Condition: During an RCI price update involving a consumer's bilateral quantity. Performing the RCI updates requires sharing the producer's current offered bilateral quantity with its communication neighbor as part of the mandatory quantity-and-price message. Scope: Producer-side quantity submission for decentralized RCI negotiation. Condition: At each RCI iteration, for a producer and its communication neighbor. Performing the RCI updates requires sharing the consumer's current requested bilateral quantity with its communication neighbor as part of the mandatory quantity-and-price message. Scope: Consumer-side quantity submission for decentralized RCI negotiation. Condition: At each RCI iteration, for a consumer and its communication neighbor. Each agent must send its bilateral price estimate to its communication neighbor as part of the prescribed information exchange. Scope: Per-iteration communication between neighboring agents in RCI negotiation. Condition: At each RCI iteration. The participants' separately calculated price estimates for a given bilateral trade must agree, λ_nm = λ_mn. Scope: Individually calculated price estimates for the same bilateral trade in the fully decentralized RCI implementation. Condition: After convergence. Reaching optimality through RCI does not require sharing agents' internal production/consumption parameters or product-differentiation criterion parameters. Scope: Information disclosure in the RCI implementation of MBED. The iterative process stops when convergence is established; convergence criterion (26) is optional. Scope: Termination of iterative RCI coordination. Condition: When algorithmic convergence is established under the prescribed stopping criteria.","target_definition":"The perceived bilateral price supplies an input to the target requested-power setpoint calculation. Scope: Target-setpoint calculation for the consumer branch of decentralized RCI negotiation. Condition: The negotiating agent acts as a consumer. Updating bilateral trading-price estimates precedes updating requested-energy decision variables within each RCI iteration. Scope: Sequence of updates within an RCI iteration, restricted to the requested-energy decision variables of consumers. Different offered prices direct the consumer to try to request as much as possible from the neighbor with the most favorable price and nothing from the others. Scope: The discussed direct-solution alternative for consumer local MBED subproblems, rather than the implemented RCI gradient update. Condition: A consumer directly solves its local subproblem when offered different prices. Requested bilateral quantities are nonpositive under the injection convention. RCI enforces this sign restriction at every iteration using the consumer min projection. Scope: Consumer requested-energy quantities in MBED and their iterative RCI updates. Condition: The agent acts as a consumer. The aggregate requested quantity, represented as the consumer's net power injection, is constrained by the agent's lower and upper power boundaries. Scope: Feasibility of consumer requested quantities in MBED. Condition: The agent acts as a consumer; the restriction concerns feasible power setpoints. The current requested bilateral quantity must be included in the information sent to the neighboring agent. Scope: Communication of consumer quantity estimates during decentralized RCI negotiation. Condition: At each iteration, for a consumer and its neighboring negotiating agent.","constraints":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R001-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Updating bilateral trading-price estimates precedes updating requested-energy decision variables within each RCI iteration. Scope: Sequence of updates within an RCI iteration, restricted to the requested-energy decision variables of consumers.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.price_signal","bidding.demand"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g01-e18","v141-b-g01-e33"]}],"evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e05","location":{"location_id":"src-8ce0608b1a-p02-c2r3__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":2,"printed_page":"995","section":"II-A. Peer-to-Peer Trading","anchor_text":"actual power network (being, e.g., transmission and distribution er grids, or possibly a microgrid),","equation_id":"(1)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-02.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"To model this trading scheme, the net power injection P_n of each agent n ∈ Ω is split into a sum of bilaterally traded quantities with a set of neighboring agents m ∈ ω_n, i.e., P_n = Σ_{m∈ω_n} P_nm (1). A positive value corresponds to a sale/production and a negative value to a purchase/consumption. The set {P_nm | n ∈ Ω, m ∈ ω_n} is the set of decision variables. To lighten notations P_n is also used for the whole set of transactions of agent n."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e18","location":{"location_id":"src-8ce0608b1a-p04-c1r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":4,"printed_page":"997","section":"II-C. MBED Formulation","anchor_text":"all trades can be made at different prices. Differences in price cen are mostly induced by product d","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The shadow prices of the reciprocity constraints (9c), denoted λ_nm, define the prices for the various trades. This implies that all trades can be made at different prices. Differences in price are mostly induced by product differentiation, but can also result from an incomplete trading graph through different price zones. Since the MBED is a convex optimization problem, it only admits a single optimum, which can be obtained by applying a wealth of centralized and distributed optimization methods."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e33","location":{"location_id":"src-8ce0608b1a-p05-c1r3__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":5,"printed_page":"998","section":"III-A. Structure of the Method","anchor_text":"prFig. 2. Flowchart of the relaxed consensus + innovation algorithm. from the others. This results i","equation_id":null,"figure_id":"Fig. 2","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"An iteration of the Relaxed Consensus + Innovation method can be split into three steps. The first two steps consist in updating the dual variables of the trading reciprocity constraints and of the power boundary constraints (III-B). The third step consists in updating the decision variables based on a gradient step built on optimality conditions of the local optimality problem (III-C). Some operational aspects are presented in III-D. The structure of the algorithm is summed up in Fig. 2."}],"omega":{"market_type":"DEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"bidding","context_text":"Communication of consumer quantity estimates during decentralized RCI negotiation. | Consumer requested-energy quantities in MBED and their iterative RCI updates. | Feasibility of consumer requested quantities in MBED. | Sequence of updates within an RCI iteration, restricted to the requested-energy decision variables of consumers. | Target-setpoint calculation for the consumer branch of decentralized RCI negotiation. | The discussed direct-solution alternative for consumer local MBED subproblems, rather than the implemented RCI gradient update.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g01-e06","v141-b-g01-e07","v141-b-g01-e18","v141-b-g01-e23","v141-b-g01-e28","v141-b-g01-e32","v141-b-g01-e33","v141-b-g02-e14","v141-b-g02-e15","v141-b-g02-e19"]},"source_record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R001-E002","source":"coordination.price_signal","target":"bidding.demand","type":"precedes","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R001-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g01-e18","v141-b-g01-e33"]},"paper_scope_note":"The λ update, P update, and required communication of RCI have direct formula basis; only protocol component dependencies are allowed, and the values of k and k+1 or the roles of consumer and producer are not conflated."}});
